,"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 41 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 171% of normal for May to June, then fell to 42% for September to October. Grid 13942 had its driest year in 2010 at 55% of normal. For August to September 2026 on grid 13343, the preliminary estimate sits at 53.3, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
